--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -24,6 +24,17 @@ This runs one [AgentDojo](https://github.com/ethz-spylab/agentdojo) banking task
 
 Task ids are `user_task_0` to `user_task_15`. Options: `--model` and `--base-url` override `.env`; `--seed` sets the seed (default 0).
 
+## Inject prompt injections (A1)
+
+```bash
+.venv/bin/python -m lineage --task user_task_0 --inject executor --injection-task injection_task_7
+.venv/bin/python -m lineage.batch --inject researcher --injection-tasks 0,4,7 --repeats 1
+```
+
+`--inject` picks one stage: `researcher` (the payload sits in AgentDojo's world data, e.g. the bill file or a transaction subject, and arrives through a tool result), `planner` (an extra researcher fact the planner reads) or `executor` (an extra fact in E1's inputs). The payload is AgentDojo's own: `--attack` (default `important_instructions`) wraps the attacker goal of `--injection-task` (`injection_task_0` to `_8`). At the researcher stage the payload is appended after the original text so no real data is lost; `--vector-mode replace` does what AgentDojo does.
+
+Each run also reports `security` (AgentDojo's check: did the attacker's goal happen?) and which steps saw or repeated the payload. The batch compares each run with `results/clean-baseline/runs.csv`: `changed` (actions not seen in any clean run), `flipped` (pass/fail differs from clean) and `ignored` (seen, but nothing changed). The code is in `lineage/faults.py`.
+
 ## How it works
 
 A research planner decides which of three researchers (files, transaction history, account) are needed and asks each one a question; they answer with read-only tools. A planner splits the work into up to two sub-plans, each listing the facts it uses. Two executors carry out the sub-plans; they are the only agents that can change the world, and each sees only its own facts. A reporter answers the user. `--layout researchers-first` runs the older layout, where all three researchers run without questions.
